# Bench uses the versioned 40-position contract and never emits bestmove.
@phase 4.3
> Manta {{VERSION}} by Miloslav Macurek
< setoption name Hash value 1
< bench 1 1 1
> {{BENCH_POSITION_LINES}}
> info string bench total depth 1 repeats 1 threads 1 nodes {{U64}} time_ms {{POSITIVE_U64}} nps {{U64}} ebf {{DECIMAL}} median_nodes {{U64}} top_share {{DECIMAL}}
! silence 100ms
< bench invalid
> info string invalid bench: depth must be a positive integer
< quit
! exit 0 within 1000ms

---

# Multiple repeats omit per-position detail and preserve run-one identity.
@phase 4.3
> Manta {{VERSION}} by Miloslav Macurek
< bench 1 2 1
> info string bench run 1/2 depth 1 threads 1 nodes {{U64}} time_ms {{U64}} nps {{U64}}
> info string bench run 2/2 depth 1 threads 1 nodes {{U64}} time_ms {{U64}} nps {{U64}}
> info string bench summary depth 1 repeats 2 threads 1 fingerprint_nodes {{U64}} best_nps {{U64}} median_nps {{U64}}
! silence 100ms
< quit
! exit 0 within 1000ms

---

# Controller-side cancellation closes the queued bench/stop epoch race.
@phase 4.3
> Manta {{VERSION}} by Miloslav Macurek
< bench 6 1 1
< stop
> info string bench cancelled run 1/1 positions {{U64}}/40 nodes {{U64}}
! silence 100ms
< quit
! exit 0 within 1000ms
